<title>GERMANY: German January metals output detailed.</title>
<headline>German January metals output detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German non-ferrous metals production in January 1997 was mostly below the same 1996 month, data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Castings figures were also mostly lower but output of semi-finished base metals products was mainly above the year earlier figure.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes --</p>
<p> METALS OUTPUT	   Jan 97    Jan 96  pct change Jan/Dec 96*</p>
<p> primary aluminium     48,682    50,361    - 3.3	 575,492</p>
<p> electrolytic copper   51,465    48,250    + 6.7	 592,415</p>
<p> zinc			25,723    27,956    - 8.0	 328,065</p>
<p> refined lead	    16,015    22,221    -27.9	 176,176</p>
<p> SEMI-FINISHED METALS  Jan 97    Jan 96  pct change Jan/Dec 96*</p>
<p> aluminium		135,586   117,530    +15.4     1,489,260</p>
<p> copper		   128,151   124,037    + 3.3     1,460,761</p>
<p> zinc			13,069    12,870    + 1.5	 172,958</p>
<p> lead			 3,730     3,801    - 1.9	  46,579</p>
<p> nickel		     1,625     1,472    +10.4	  17,722</p>
<p> METALS CASTINGS	 Jan 97    Jan 96  pct change Jan/Dec 96*</p>
<p> aluminium		 42,671    43,083    - 1.0	 475,621</p>
<p> copper		     6,606     6,711    - 1.6	  71,216</p>
<p> zinc			 5,590     5,809    - 3.8	  62,862</p>
<p> lead			   532	 715    -25.6	   6,296</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel and tin castings data were not given.</p>
<p>*revised data</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
